"\n\n\n\n\n## Ordered\n\n\n\n## Review\nI got a strong sense that this restaurant puts tremendous effort into the buckwheat aroma.  \n\nThe Buckwheat Noodles were subtly delicious — not pungent at all, yet the distinctive buckwheat fragrance came through beautifully.  \nThe broth was light and not overpowering, and I appreciated the overall restrained seasoning style.  \n\nThe Wild Greens Buckwheat Noodles were impressive — clearly in the perilla oil noodle style, with the nutty aroma coming through strong.  \nThe wild greens and perilla oil paired so well together that, if you're not set on having cold noodles, I'd recommend this one over the other.  \nThat said, both were delicious.  \n\nThe Potato Pancake was , not the chewy kind.  \nIt seemed made with potato alone, so the natural ingredient aroma was pleasant and non-pungent — a great pairing with the buckwheat noodles.  \n\nI wanted to order a large size, but held back because of the potato pancake.  \nLooking back after finishing everything, I think I could have gone for the large size after all.  \n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n"